      "before": "An API that accepts product images has the backend choose the member and a single key for each upload. The browser should PUT directly using a signed request, without obtaining credentials, and its upload permission should expire after 10 minutes.",
      "after": "An API that accepts product images needs the backend to identify the member and select a single key for each upload. The browser should PUT directly using a signed request, without obtaining credentials, and its upload permission should expire after 10 minutes.",
      "reason": "“Choose the member” inaccurately implies the backend selects a user; “identify the member” conveys determining which member is authenticated while preserving the per-upload key, signed request, credential exclusion, and 10-minute expiration.",
      "decision": "refined",
      "final": "An API accepts product images. Its backend identifies the member and selects a single destination key for each upload. The browser should PUT directly using a signed request, without obtaining credentials, and its upload permission should expire after 10 minutes.",
      "reasonMain": "識別するという提案を採用し、APIとbackendの関係を2文で自然に表す。署名PUT/認証情報なし/10分/一つのキーという原条件を保持。"
    }
